{
  "capitulo": 7,
  "titulo_es": "Si tuviera tiempo",
  "titulo": { "en": "If I had time" },
  "intro": { "en": "A hypothetical if uses the imperfect subjunctive and the conditional." },
  "palabras": {
    "si": { "en": "if", "pron": "si", "cat": "conjunction" },
    "tuviera": { "en": "I/he/she had (hypothetical)", "pron": "tu-BYE-ra", "cat": "verb" },
    "fuera": { "en": "I/he/she were", "pron": "FWE-ra", "cat": "verb" },
    "viajaría": { "en": "I/he/she would travel", "pron": "bya-ha-RI-a", "cat": "verb" },
    "hablaría": { "en": "I/he/she would speak", "pron": "a-bla-RI-a", "cat": "verb" },
    "tendría": { "en": "I/he/she would have", "pron": "ten-DRI-a", "cat": "verb" },
    "tiempo": { "en": "time", "pron": "TYEM-po", "genero": "m" },
    "dinero": { "en": "money", "pron": "di-NE-ro", "genero": "m" }
  },
  "bloques": [
    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": "Real, or imagined",
      "texto": "A real possibility stays in the ordinary present.\n\n- **Si tengo** tiempo, voy.\n\nAn imagined present uses the imperfect subjunctive and the conditional.\n\n- **Si tuviera** tiempo, **viajaría**.\n- **Si fuera** tú, **hablaría** con ella.\n\nThe conditional ending is **-ía** on the infinitive: hablaría, comería, viviría. Ir and tener change: **iría**, **tendría**."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "dialogo",
      "titulo": "If",
      "frases": [
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "Si tengo tiempo, voy al cine.",
          "en": "If I have time, I go to the cinema.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Si tengo tiempo", "real condition"],
            ["voy al cine", "I go to the cinema"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Pablo",
          "es": "Si tuviera tiempo, viajaría.",
          "en": "If I had time, I would travel.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Si tuviera tiempo", "hypothetical"],
            ["viajaría", "I would travel"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Lucía",
          "es": "Si tuviera dinero, tendría una casa.",
          "en": "If I had money, I would have a house.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Si tuviera dinero", "if I had money"],
            ["tendría", "I would have"],
            ["una casa", "a house"]
          ]
        },
        {
          "quien": "Pablo",
          "es": "Si yo fuera tú, hablaría con ella.",
          "en": "If I were you, I would speak to her.",
          "analisis": [
            ["Si yo fuera tú", "if I were you"],
            ["hablaría", "I would speak"],
            ["con ella", "with her"]
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "vocabulario",
      "palabras": ["si", "tuviera", "fuera", "viajaría", "hablaría", "tendría", "tiempo", "dinero"]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "test",
      "id": "b2-si-hipotesis",
      "pregunta": { "en": "Which sentence is only imagined?" },
      "opciones": {
        "Si tuviera tiempo, viajaría": { "en": "Tuviera plus the conditional is hypothetical." },
        "Si tengo tiempo, voy": { "en": "That is a real, possible plan." },
        "Cuando tengo tiempo, leo": { "en": "That is a habit." }
      },
      "correcta": "Si tuviera tiempo, viajaría"
    },
    {
      "tipo": "huecos",
      "id": "b2-si-viajaria",
      "pregunta": { "en": "Complete the imagined result." },
      "frase": "Si tuviera tiempo, ___.",
      "audio": true,
      "opciones": {
        "viajaría": { "en": "The result of an imagined if is the conditional." },
        "viajo": { "en": "Viajo is the real present." },
        "viajé": { "en": "Viajé is the past." }
      },
      "correcta": "viajaría"
    }
  ]
}
